From 6c00db351c3edaabd708294bd9b702b07f66cb4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 02:29:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: mark floor lighting from the game in the map update

The map update's Floors branch tested g.f_idx == FEAT_NONE, the same
condition as the Darkness branch before it in the same else-if chain,
so it was never taken: floor grids were never marked BORG_GLOW,
BORG_DARK or BORG_LIGHT from the game's lighting. The condition is a
transcription slip from the original borg's switch, which cased
FEAT_FLOOR here.

Restore the FEAT_FLOOR condition, and read the glow state from
square_islit() -- the grid's permanent-glow flag, matching the
CAVE_GLOW test the original branch performed. The grid_data lighting
enum cannot express glow: LIGHTING_LIT is map_info's default value for
grids whose lighting is not otherwise established, so the transcribed
g.lighting == LIGHTING_LIT test would have marked remembered dark
floors as glowing.

Consumers: the borg's flow-toward-light builds its target list purely
from BORG_GLOW grids and returned empty on every level; unlit-Borg
defense checks treat !BORG_GLOW grids as dark. With the correction, a
permanently glowing floor away from the borg's own torch radius is
flagged glowing, an unlit floor is flagged dark, and walls and doors
are untouched.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#213.
---
 src/borg/borg-update.c | 21 +++++++++------------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-update.c b/src/borg/borg-update.c
index 6cd7a85e6..83ed702db 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-update.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-update.c
@@ -362,35 +362,32 @@ static void borg_update_map(void)
                     ag->info |= BORG_DARK;
             }
             /* Floors */
-            else if (g.f_idx == FEAT_NONE) {
+            else if (g.f_idx == FEAT_FLOOR) {
                 /* Handle "blind" */
                 if (borg.trait[BI_ISBLIND]) {
                     /* Nothing */
                 }
 
-                /* Handle "dark" floors */
-                if (g.lighting == LIGHTING_DARK) {
+                /* Handle "dark" floors.  square_islit() is the grid's
+                 * permanent-glow flag, matching the CAVE_GLOW test this
+                 * branch transcribed from the original borg; the lighting
+                 * enum in grid_data cannot express it (LIGHTING_LIT is
+                 * map_info's default for grids whose lighting is not
+                 * otherwise established). */
+                if (!square_islit(cave, l)) {
                     /* Dark floor grid */
                     ag->info |= BORG_DARK;
                     ag->info &= ~BORG_GLOW;
                 }
 
                 /* Handle Glowing floors */
-                else if (g.lighting == LIGHTING_LIT) {
+                else {
                     /* Perma Glowing Grid */
                     ag->info |= BORG_GLOW;
 
                     /* Assume not dark */
                     ag->info &= ~BORG_DARK;
                 }
-
-                /* torch-lit or line of sight grids */
-                else {
-                    ag->info |= BORG_LIGHT;
-
-                    /* Assume not dark */
-                    ag->info &= ~BORG_DARK;
-                }
             }
             /* Open doors */
             else if (g.f_idx == FEAT_OPEN || g.f_idx == FEAT_BROKEN) {
